**1. A system for attributing web orders to media airings, the system comprising:**

one or more processors; and

memory storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the system to:

receive, from one or more media-airing data sources, airing records respectively identifying media airings, each airing record including a media identifier, a distribution channel, and an airing time;

receive, from a web-commerce platform, order event data representing web orders, each web order being associated with an order time and at least one order attribute;

normalize the airing times and the order times to a common time reference;

for each web order, identify, from the airing records, a set of candidate media airings having respective airing times within a predetermined attribution interval preceding the order time;

generate, for each candidate media airing, an attribution score based at least in part on a temporal relationship between the airing time and the order time and a correspondence between the at least one order attribute and information associated with the candidate media airing;

select, according to the attribution scores and an attribution rule, a particular media airing from the set of candidate media airings;

store an attribution record associating the web order with the particular media airing;

increment, based on the attribution record, at least one attribution metric maintained for the particular media airing; and

cause a client device to display an attribution report identifying the particular media airing and the at least one attribution metric, wherein the attribution report is updated in real time in response to receipt and attribution of additional web orders.
